<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P21217">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Galactoside 3(4)-L-fucosyltransferase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P21217" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_FUT3_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUT3_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Blood group Lewis alpha-4-fucosyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Fucosyltransferase III</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.4.1.65</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LE</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FT3B</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FucT-III</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Lewis FT</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Fucosyltransferase 3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUT3</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference124741</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUT3_HUMAN Reviewed; 361 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot/A8K737</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: May catalyze alpha-1,3 and alpha-1,4 glycosidic linkagesinvolved in the expression of Vim-2, Lewis A, Lewis B, sialylLewis X and Lewis X/SSEA-1 antigens. May be involved in bloodgroup Lewis determination; Lewis-positive (Le(+)) individuals havean active enzyme while Lewis-negative (Le(-)) individuals have aninactive enzyme. Also acts on the corresponding 1,4-galactosylderivative, forming 1,3-L-fucosyl links.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=a beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;3)-N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminylderivative + GDP-beta-L-fucose = a beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;3)-[alpha-L-fucosyl-(1-&gt;4)]-N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl derivative+ GDP + H(+); Xref=Rhea:RHEA:23628, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:57273, ChEBI:CHEBI:58189, ChEBI:CHEBI:133506,ChEBI:CHEBI:140304; EC=2.4.1.65;PATHWAY: Protein modification; protein glycosylation.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Golgi apparatus, Golgi stack membrane;Single-pass type II membrane protein. Note=Membrane-bound form intrans cisternae of Golgi.TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in stomach, colon, smallintestine, lung and kidney and to a lesser extent in salivarygland, bladder, uterus and liver.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase 10 family.{ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=dbRBC/BGMUT; Note=Blood group antigen genemutation database;URL=&quot;https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gv/mhc/xslcgi.cgi?cmd=bgmut/systems_info&amp;system=lewis&quot;;WEB RESOURCE: Name=SeattleSNPs;URL=&quot;http://pga.gs.washington.edu/data/fut3/&quot;;WEB RESOURCE: Name=Functional Glycomics Gateway - GTase;Note=Fucosyltransferase 3;URL=&quot;http://www.functionalglycomics.org/glycomics/molecule/jsp/glycoEnzyme/viewGlycoEnzyme.jsp?gbpId=gt_hum_600&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_2525</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

