<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q9BYG0">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Lactosylceramide 1,3-N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyltransferase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_B3GNT5_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q9BYG0" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">B3GN5_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UDP-GlcNAc:beta-Gal beta-1,3-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase 5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta3Gn-T5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Lc3 synthase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">B3GNT5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">BGnT-5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Lc(3)Cer synthase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-1,3-Gn-T5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-1,3-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase 5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Lactotriaosylceramide synthase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.4.1.206</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">B3GN5_HUMAN Reviewed; 378 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_114436</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_84002</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Beta-1,3-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase that plays akey role in the synthesis of lacto- or neolacto-seriescarbohydrate chains on glycolipids, notably by participating inbiosynthesis of HNK-1 and Lewis X carbohydrate structures. Hasstrong activity toward lactosylceramide (LacCer) andneolactotetraosylceramide (nLc(4)Cer; paragloboside), resulting inthe synthesis of Lc(3)Cer and neolactopentaosylceramide(nLc(5)Cer), respectively. Probably plays a central role inregulating neolacto-series glycolipid synthesis during embryonicdevelopment.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-glucosyl-(1&lt;-&gt;1)-ceramide(d18:1(4E)) + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine = beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;3)-beta-D-Gal-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-Glc-(1&lt;-&gt;1)-N-acylsphing-4-enine + H(+) + UDP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:13905, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:17103, ChEBI:CHEBI:17950, ChEBI:CHEBI:57705,ChEBI:CHEBI:58223; EC=2.4.1.206;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:11283017};PATHWAY: Protein modification; protein glycosylation.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Golgi apparatus membrane {ECO:0000250};Single-pass type II membrane protein {ECO:0000250}.TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Widely expressed. Highly expressed in lung,colon, placenta, testis, pituitary gland and cerebellum. Weaklyexpressed in brain, liver, spleen, lymph node and thymus.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:11283017}.INDUCTION: Up-regulated by stimulation with retinoic acid anddown-regulated with 12-O-tetradecanoylphorbol-13-acetate (TPA).{ECO:0000269|PubMed:11283017}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase 31 family.{ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=BAD92754.1; Type=Frameshift; Positions=347; Evidence={ECO:0000305};WEB RESOURCE: Name=Functional Glycomics Gateway - GTase;Note=Beta1,3-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase 5;URL=&quot;http://www.functionalglycomics.org/glycomics/molecule/jsp/glycoEnzyme/viewGlycoEnzyme.jsp?gbpId=gt_hum_538&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

